Tom Holub (tom@soda.berkeley.edu) wrote:
: Now, you can say, 'don't use wishes or polypiling or rings of conflict',
: but that ignores the fact that someone who doesn't feel the same way
: you do about the game can fill up the high score list with easily-earned
: winners.  The most important factor in game design is balance; the most
: difficult thing to do when designing games is balance them.  To put
: out an unbalanced game and then say 'don't do the things that make 
: it too easy' is wrong.

IMHO the most important factor in game design is fun factor.  I don't
care who gets the highest score, I like the game to be fun.  Perhaps we
need something between explore mode, where you start with a WoW, and
the regular game.  Perhaps we can set the difficulty level by
enabling/disabling certain tricks like polypiling, rings of conflict,
certain shop robbing tricks, etc.  Taking out those tricks could affect
some fun aspect of the game.  Variety is the spice of life.  Making the
game with various "tricks" might give a gamer more various ways to win
the game.

